course: dictionary
lesson: 7996
title: Redden: when things turn red
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Redden» is a verb, so it describes something that happens or something you do. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The reddening apples» and «rowans were reddening» both describe something turning red, like fruit and berries ripening in late summer.
explain: Redden can also describe a person. When someone's face reddens, they are embarrassed, shy or angry. In a story, «his face reddened» tells you how the character feels, not just what colour his face is.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The apples became red» still makes sense, so redden means become red. «The apples became green» does not fit the clues, so green is not the answer.
fact: «Redden» means to become red or redder.
fact: When your face reddens, you blush, usually from embarrassment, shyness or anger.
fact: Redden can also mean to make something red.
fact: Redden is a verb: redden, reddens, reddened, reddening.
fact: «Rowans were reddening» means the rowan berries were turning red as summer ended.
exercise: «The reddening apples hung in the orchard.» What does reddening mean here? | *Becoming red | Falling to the ground | Turning green | Being picked and eaten
exercise: «Her face reddened when everyone laughed at her mistake.» What does this tell us? | She was singing loudly | *She felt embarrassed | Her face was cold | She was fast asleep
exercise: Which word is a form of redden? | *reddens | red | ruddy | rosy
test: «Tom's cheeks reddened with anger.» What does reddened mean here? | Went pale | Went outside | Went to sleep | *Went red
test: «The leaves reddened in autumn.» What is happening to the leaves? | They are turning green | They are falling off | *They are becoming red | They are being painted
exam: «The sky reddened as the sun set.» What does reddened mean? | Became noisy | Became dark and grey | *Became red | Became bigger
